From: plotarmordev <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:13:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 19/30] drama: one-row backbone GEMVs stream weights through a
 swizzled cp.async ring

The one-row path keeps the same mma sequence and fragments as the tilings it replaces, now for the semantic
head's grouping too, while its weights stream through an unpadded shared ring whose 16-byte pieces are swizzled
so each read still hits distinct banks.
